	'i_prog_0_a' => 'Diploma in Early Years Practice: how to apply',
	'i_prog_0_b_0' => 'The Diploma in Early Years Practice is a two-year full-time course designed for school leavers and career changers seeking comprehensive preparation for early-childhood classrooms. The cohort is capped at 24 trainees, divided into two intimate seminar groups of 12. Trainees spend Mondays and Tuesdays in partner settings, Wednesdays and Thursdays at college, and Fridays in guided self-study. Applicants must complete an initial visit, submit a 400-word statement with one reference, and attend an observed morning in May. The curriculum covers six core modules: Child Development in the Early Years, The Observation of Play, Language and Storytelling, Studio Materials and the Senses, Outdoor Environments, and Professional Practice in Early Childhood. Tuition is €6,400 per year.',
	'i_prog_0_price' => 'Tuition: €6,400 per year',
	'i_prog_1_time' => 'One year, full-time',
	'i_prog_1_h' => 'Graduate Certificate in Early Years Teaching',
	'i_prog_1_p' => 'For people who already hold a degree. Placements in nurseries and reception classes. Cohort of 12.',
	'i_prog_1_a' => 'Graduate Certificate in Early Years Teaching: how to apply',
	'i_prog_1_b_0' => 'The Graduate Certificate in Early Years Teaching provides an intensive one-year full-time route for individuals who already hold an undergraduate degree in any subject. With a cohort strictly limited to 12 students, this pathway moves swiftly between nursery environments and primary school reception classrooms. Trainees spend two days each week in partner settings and two days at college, examining pedagogy and curriculum design. Entry requires an existing bachelor\'s degree, a 400-word personal statement, one reference, and participation in an observed morning. The six modules comprise Advanced Child Development, Pedagogy of Reception Classrooms, Early Literacy and Numeracy, Observation and Assessment, Supporting Diverse Learning Needs, and Leadership in Early Years Settings. Tuition is €7,200.',
	'i_prog_1_price' => 'Tuition: €7,200',
	'i_prog_2_time' => 'Two and a half years, part-time',
	'i_prog_2_h' => 'Weekend Route for Working Assistants',
	'i_prog_2_p' => 'Saturdays 09:00–15:00 at college, and your own setting during the week. Cohort of 16.',
	'i_prog_2_a' => 'Weekend Route for Working Assistants: how to apply',
	'i_prog_2_b_0' => 'The Weekend Route for Working Assistants is a 2½-year part-time programme tailored for classroom assistants already employed in early-years settings. Cohorts are limited to 16 students, split into two seminar groups of eight, who attend college on Saturdays from 09:00 to 15:00 while continuing their regular paid employment during the week. Practical observation takes place within their home nursery or school setting. Applicants must have current employment in an early-years classroom, supportive employer agreement, a 400-word statement, and one reference. The programme features six modules: Workplace Observation and Practice, The Developing Child, Communication and Relationships, Expressive Arts and Movement, Collaborative Practice with Families, and The Reflective Practitioner. Tuition is €3,900 per year, payable in three annual instalments.',
	'i_prog_2_price' => 'Tuition: €3,900 per year',
	'i_prog_fees' => 'See the full fee sheet',
	'i_place_hero_pill' => 'Placements',
	'i_place_hero_lead' => 'Practical experience begins in week 3 across our network of 14 partner nurseries and reception classes. Trainees spend two days each week immersed in classroom life under the guidance of room leads and visiting tutors.',
	'i_place_s0_pill' => 'From week 3',
	'i_place_s0_h' => 'How placements work from week 3',
	'i_place_s0_b_0' => 'Placements begin promptly in week 3 of the autumn term, ensuring trainees build relationships with children and staff from the very beginning of the school year. Every trainee spends two full days each week in a partner classroom, taking responsibility for a key group of six children. Rather than drifting through room routines, you observe and support these six children closely, learning their individual rhythms, friendships, and developmental steps. Once a week, a college practice tutor visits your room to watch you work for an hour, taking notes from the doorway. Later that same afternoon, you meet the tutor at college for a focused tutorial to review what occurred and plan purposeful adjustments.',
	'i_place_c0_time' => '9 settings',
	'i_place_c0_h' => 'Day nurseries',
	'i_place_c0_p' => 'Children from two to four, key groups of six, and low tables where you sit with them.',
	'i_place_c0_a' => 'Day nurseries: a day on the course',
	'i_place_c1_time' => '5 settings',
	'i_place_c1_h' => 'Reception classes',
	'i_place_c1_p' => 'A school class of four- and five-year-olds, with a class teacher beside you.',
	'i_place_c1_a' => 'Reception classes: programmes',
	'i_place_s1_pill' => 'Two kinds of setting',
	'i_place_s1_h' => 'Nurseries and reception classes: two distinct learning environments',
	'i_place_s1_b_0' => 'Our network of 14 partner settings divides into nine day nurseries and five school reception classes, ensuring balanced exposure to infant, toddler, and pre-school stages. The nine nurseries, including Little Oak Day Nursery and Brookside Nursery, focus on toddlers and young children aged two to four. Here, trainees explore free-flow play, emotional security, and sensory routines. The five reception classes, such as Hollins Lane Primary, introduce the structure of the first statutory school year for four- and five-year-olds. In reception, trainees learn how teachers balance exploratory inquiry with emerging literacy and numeracy. Experiencing both settings equips educators to understand the full continuum of early childhood across statutory and community care.',
	'i_place_t3a_l' => 'Brookside',
	'i_place_t3a_s' => 'Nursery',
	'i_place_t3a_a' => 'Brookside Nursery: meet the tutors',
	'i_place_t3a_t' => 'A day nursery with a mud kitchen at the back. Trainees join a key group in week 3, and Tomas Lindgren visits before every placement begins.',
	'i_place_t3b_l' => 'Hollins Lane',
	'i_place_t3b_s' => 'Primary',
	'i_place_t3b_a' => 'Hollins Lane Primary: graduate stories',
	'i_place_t3b_t' => 'A primary school whose reception class takes Graduate Certificate trainees. One of our graduates now teaches there.',
	'i_place_o0' => 'Fernhill Forest Nursery',
	'i_place_o1' => 'Little Oak Day Nursery',
	'i_place_o2' => 'Calder Street Children’s Centre',
	'i_place_o3' => 'and nine more nurseries and reception classes within 25 minutes of the campus',
	'i_place_s2_pill' => 'Partner settings',
	'i_place_s2_h' => 'Our partner settings: Brookside Nursery, Hollins Lane Primary, and beyond',
	'i_place_s2_b_0' => 'Placements are coordinated by Tomas Lindgren, who matches each student with a setting suited to their commute and developmental interests. Longstanding settings include Brookside Nursery, celebrated for its attentive toddler care, and Hollins Lane Primary, where reception trainees observe balanced early classroom teaching. Trainees also spend placement days at Fernhill Forest Nursery with its outdoor woodland curriculum, Little Oak Day Nursery, and Calder Street Children\'s Centre. The remaining nine partner settings span community pre-schools, rural infant nurseries, and municipal reception rooms across the Calder Downs. Every setting sits within 25 minutes of 2 Orchard Row, maintaining seamless communication between classroom mentors and our college faculty.',
	'i_tut_hero_pill' => 'The tutors',
	'i_tut_hero_lead' => 'Our faculty combines active floor experience with a commitment to close, individual mentorship. Tutors teach on campus and regularly visit partner nurseries to observe trainees working alongside children.',
	'i_tut_s0_pill' => 'Who teaches you',
	'i_tut_s0_h' => 'Leadership and practice mentorship',
	'i_tut_s0_b_0' => 'Principal Clara Benedetti leads Mebuki College with deep roots in early-years education, having taught reception classes for 14 years before becoming principal in 2016. She oversees college curriculum and maintains our institutional focus on calm, child-centred practice. Practice tutor Ines Adeyemi visits partner classrooms weekly with her notebook, observing trainees on the floor and leading reflective afternoon tutorials at Orchard Row. Her mentoring helps trainees notice subtle cues in children\'s interactions. Tomas Lindgren serves as head of placements, stewarding relationships across our 14 partner nurseries and reception classes throughout the Calder Downs. Tomas works closely with room leads to ensure each trainee receives steady, attentive supervision on placement days.',
	'i_tut_m0_l' => 'Ines',
	'i_tut_m0_s' => 'Practice tutor',
	'i_tut_m0_a' => 'Ines: placements',
	'i_tut_m0_t' => 'Ines watches trainees from the doorway of a partner nursery and talks it through with each of them the same afternoon. She writes down what the child did first.',
	'i_tut_m1_l' => 'Owen',
	'i_tut_m1_s' => 'Studio and garden',
	'i_tut_m1_a' => 'Owen: placements',
	'i_tut_m1_t' => 'Owen runs the studio and the garden work: sand, water, clay and mud. He asks trainees to try every activity themselves, and teaches the Saturday short course.',
	'i_tut_m2_l' => 'Tomas',
	'i_tut_m2_s' => 'Placements',
	'i_tut_m2_a' => 'Tomas: placements',
	'i_tut_m2_t' => 'Tomas looks after the 14 partner settings. He matches each trainee to a nursery or reception class within reach of home and visits every setting before a placement begins.',
	'i_tut_m3_l' => 'Clara',
	'i_tut_m3_s' => 'Principal',
	'i_tut_m3_t' => 'Clara taught reception classes for fourteen years and has been principal since 2016. She still spends a morning a week in a partner setting and reads every observation report.',
	'i_tut_p0_l' => 'Hannah',
	'i_tut_p0_s' => 'Child development',
	'i_tut_p0_t' => 'Hannah Weiss teaches the Wednesday seminar on how children learn, linking what trainees saw on Tuesday to what is known about play, language and attention.',
	'i_tut_p1_l' => 'Rafael',
	'i_tut_p1_s' => 'Music and movement',
	'i_tut_p1_t' => 'Rafael Ortega leads the Thursday studio of songs, rhythm and movement, and shows trainees how to use voice and body with children who are not yet reading.',
	'i_tut_p2_l' => 'Priya',
	'i_tut_p2_s' => 'Admissions',
	'i_tut_p2_t' => 'Priya Raman answers every application and every question about applying. She meets visitors at the door on open days and arranges each observed morning.',
	'i_tut_s1_pill' => 'The wider team',
	'i_tut_s1_h' => 'Child development, studio arts, and admissions',
	'i_tut_s1_b_0' => 'Hannah Weiss lectures in child development, guiding weekly seminars that link psychological research to real morning classroom observations. In the college studio, Rafael Ortega leads workshops in music and movement, demonstrating how rhythm, song, and physical games foster young children\'s expressive communication. Owen Gallagher oversees the college studio and outdoor-learning environments, teaching practical courses on sand, water, clay, and mud exploration in our garden and at Fernhill Forest Nursery. Admissions officer Priya Raman personally handles every application and inquiry, guiding prospective trainees through Wednesday afternoon tours, Saturday open days, and interview morning bookings. Together, our team ensures every student receives personal attention throughout their studies.',
	'i_tut_v_time' => 'Once a week',
	'i_tut_v_h' => 'How a tutor visit works',
	'i_tut_v_p' => 'Your tutor watches from the doorway, takes notes, and talks it through with you the same afternoon.',
	'i_tut_v_a' => 'How a tutor visit works: placements',
	'i_tut_s2_pill' => 'The weekly visit',
	'i_tut_s2_h' => 'How does a weekly tutor visit work?',
	'i_tut_s2_b_0' => 'Every tutor visit is structured to be constructive rather than judgmental. Once a week during placement days, your practice tutor arrives at your partner setting and takes a quiet seat in the doorway or room corner. For an hour, the tutor observes your floor work with your key group of six children, recording notes on interactions, spoken language, transitions, and material use. The tutor does not intervene unless requested. Later that afternoon at Orchard Row, you sit down together with mugs of tea to read through the written observations. You discuss moments of engagement, reflect on challenging interactions, and agree on practical strategies to test during your next placement morning.',
	'i_adm_hero_pill' => 'Admissions',
	'i_adm_hero_lead' => 'We admit small cohorts of dedicated individuals ready to learn beside young children. Our four-step admissions process focuses on practical aptitude, observation skills, and genuine commitment to early-years care.',
	'i_adm_s0_pill' => 'How to apply',
	'i_adm_s0_h' => 'Our four-step application process',
	'i_adm_s0_b_0' => 'Admission to Mebuki College follows four clear steps designed to ensure mutual fit. First, prospective students visit our campus by attending a Saturday open day or a Wednesday tour between 14:00 and 15:30. Second, applicants submit a 400-word personal statement and one reference by the 30 April 2027 deadline, describing their interest in early-childhood education. Third, invited candidates take part in an observed morning during May, spending half a day in a partner nursery alongside a tutor, followed by a 30-minute reflective conversation. Fourth, formal offers are issued within 10 working days. Following a standard background check, candidates confirm their place by paying a €300 deposit, which is credited toward first-year tuition.',
	'i_adm_s1_pill' => 'The observed morning',
	'i_adm_s1_h' => 'What happens during the observed morning?',
	'i_adm_s1_b_0' => 'The observed morning replaces conventional panel interviews with real classroom practice. You spend half a day in a partner nursery room working with toddlers and young children under natural daily conditions. Candidates should wear comfortable, washable clothing suitable for floor play, sand trays, and garden activities, and bring an observation notebook. A practice tutor watches unobtrusively to assess how comfortably you communicate with young children, listen to their ideas, and respond to classroom rhythms. Following the morning session, you meet the tutor for a 30-minute conversation to discuss what you noticed. This conversation explores your reflective capacity rather than encyclopaedic knowledge of pedagogy, ensuring candidate readiness for September.',
	'i_adm_s2_pill' => 'Dates and fees',
	'i_adm_s2_h' => 'Key dates, fees, and confirming your place',
	'i_adm_s2_b_0' => 'Important dates for the 2027 intake include our open days on Saturday 16 January 2027 and Saturday 13 March 2027 (10:00–13:00). Applications for all routes close on 30 April 2027. Observed mornings take place throughout May, and the autumn term begins on Monday 6 September 2027, with partner placements commencing on 20 September 2027. The application and interview fee is €40. Tuition fees are €6,400 per year for the Diploma, €7,200 for the Graduate Certificate, and €3,900 per year for the Weekend Route, payable in three annual instalments. A €300 deposit confirms your place upon offer. To begin, visit our open days page or contact Priya Raman in admissions.',
	'i_adm_fees' => 'See the full fee sheet',
	'i_fees_hero_pill' => 'Fees and funding',
	'i_fees_hero_lead' => 'Tuition at Mebuki College covers all classroom seminars, weekly tutor visits on placement, and access to campus studios and library facilities. We offer clear fee structures payable in three instalments each year.',
	'i_fees_s0_pill' => 'The fee sheet',
	'i_fees_s0_h' => 'Tuition fee sheet for 2027',
	'i_fees_s1_pill' => 'Paying',
	'i_fees_s1_h' => 'Payment instalments and deposit details',
	'i_fees_s1_b_0' => 'A deposit of €300 confirms acceptance of an offered place and is counted directly toward your first year\'s tuition fees. To assist students with budgeting, annual course fees can be divided into three equal instalments across the academic year, timed to coincide with the start of the autumn, spring, and summer terms. Application fees of €40 cover personal statement assessment, reference verification, and the half-day observed morning with a tutor. First-year trainees also purchase the €180 placement kit, which includes two durable cotton aprons, bound observation notebooks, and certification through our mandatory paediatric first-aid training course before nursery work begins.',
	'i_fees_c_time' => 'What fees pay for',
	'i_fees_c_h' => 'Seminars, studio, one visit a week',
	'i_fees_c_p' => 'Teaching at Orchard Row, studio materials, the library and a tutor in the doorway of your placement.',
	'i_fees_c_a' => 'What fees pay for: programmes',
	'i_fees_s2_pill' => 'What is covered',
	'i_fees_s2_h' => 'What do your tuition fees cover?',
	'i_fees_s2_b_0' => 'Tuition fees fund the complete academic and practical structure of your course. This includes all weekly lectures and seminars at 2 Orchard Row, regular materials used in the college studio (such as clay, paints, sand, and wood), full library access, and weekly one-to-one observation visits by practice tutors in partner classrooms. Tuition also covers individual tutorial debriefs and assessment of professional portfolios. Tuition does not cover everyday travel expenses incurred commuting to partner nurseries across the Calder Downs, nor does it cover personal copies of textbooks trainees may choose to purchase for their own libraries. Trainees are encouraged to use campus library copies for required course readings.',
	'i_story_hero_pill' => 'Graduate stories',
	'i_story_hero_lead' => 'Graduates of Mebuki College work in nurseries, reception classrooms, and outdoor forest settings throughout the Calder Downs. Here, four alumni reflect on their training, the hardest weeks, and where they teach now.',
	'i_story_0_l' => 'Amina',
	'i_story_0_s' => 'Weekend 2022',
	'i_story_0_a' => 'Amina: programmes',
	'i_story_0_t' => '"The Saturday seminars allowed me to connect daily room observations with deeper developmental principles," explains Amina Farouk, who completed the Weekend Route in 2022. Amina started as a classroom assistant at Little Oak Day Nursery; her hardest week involved balancing full-time employment with portfolio writing during winter observations. Today, she serves as deputy head at Little Oak Day Nursery, mentoring new trainees.',
	'i_story_1_l' => 'Daniel',
	'i_story_1_s' => 'Certificate 2024',
	'i_story_1_a' => 'Daniel: programmes',
	'i_story_1_t' => 'Daniel Kowalski completed the Graduate Certificate in 2024 after holding a university degree. "Learning to quiet my voice and watch children solve physical puzzles transformed my classroom management," Daniel recalls. His most demanding week came during November transitions in reception. Daniel now works as a full-time reception class teacher at Hollins Lane Primary, guiding early numeracy and play.',
	'i_story_2_l' => 'Joanna',
	'i_story_2_s' => 'Diploma 2021',
	'i_story_2_a' => 'Joanna: programmes',
	'i_story_2_t' => '"Spending entire mornings outdoors in wet weather taught me how resilience grows through unhurried contact with nature," says Joanna Price, a 2021 Diploma graduate. Joanna arrived at college with no prior childcare experience; her hardest week was navigating outdoor winter rain while documenting child-initiated construction. Today, Joanna leads outdoor morning sessions at Fernhill Forest Nursery.',
	'i_story_3_l' => 'Samir',
	'i_story_3_s' => 'Diploma 2023',
	'i_story_3_a' => 'Samir: programmes',
	'i_story_3_t' => 'Samir Haddad finished the two-year Diploma in 2023 after changing careers. "Ines showed me that observing two-year-olds requires watching posture, hands, and breathing rather than waiting for words," notes Samir. His most challenging period was his first month handling toddler separation anxiety. Samir is currently room lead for the two-year-olds at Brookside Nursery, fostering calm, confident group play.',
	'i_story_g_pill' => 'Where they work now',
	'i_story_g_h' => 'Four graduates, four settings',
	'i_story_more' => 'Come to an open day',
	'i_open_hero_pill' => 'Open days',
	'i_open_hero_lead' => 'Visiting 2 Orchard Row is the best way to experience our calm teaching rooms, meet faculty, and observe our educational approach. We hold two dedicated Saturday open days and regular Wednesday afternoon tours.',
	'i_open_s0_pill' => 'Two Saturdays',
	'i_open_s0_h' => 'Saturday open days: schedule and morning timetable',
	'i_open_s0_b_0' => 'Our dedicated Saturday open days take place on 16 January 2027 and 13 March 2027, running from 10:00 to 13:00 at 2 Orchard Row in Hollins. The morning timetable gives prospective applicants a true taste of our learning community:
- 10:00 Welcome tea and introductory remarks with Principal Clara Benedetti.
- 10:20 Hands-on studio session with Owen Gallagher exploring sand, water, and natural materials.
- 11:15 Small-group talk with practice tutor Ines Adeyemi about weekly placement observations.
- 12:00 Admissions and course questions with admissions officer Priya Raman.
- 13:00 Close of the morning.
Visitors are encouraged to wear comfortable clothing to participate freely in the studio workshop.',
	'i_open_tt0_t' => '10:00',
	'i_open_tt0_l' => 'Welcome at the door',
	'i_open_tt1_t' => '10:20',
	'i_open_tt1_l' => 'A studio session with Owen Gallagher',
	'i_open_tt2_t' => '11:15',
	'i_open_tt2_l' => 'A talk with a practice tutor',
	'i_open_tt3_t' => '12:00',
	'i_open_tt3_l' => 'Questions with Priya Raman',
	'i_open_tt4_t' => '13:00',
	'i_open_tt4_l' => 'Close',
	'i_open_tt_pill' => 'The morning',
	'i_open_tt_h' => 'The Saturday timetable',
	'i_open_s1_pill' => 'Wednesday tours',
	'i_open_s1_h' => 'Wednesday afternoon tours and booking your visit',
	'i_open_s1_b_0' => 'For those unable to attend a Saturday open day, we offer guided campus tours every Wednesday afternoon from 14:00 to 15:30 throughout term time. Wednesday visitors see seminar groups in progress, walk through the studio and garden, and meet tutors in an unhurried setting. To reserve your place for a Saturday open day or a Wednesday tour, complete our online booking form selecting your preferred date and programme. Alternatively, book by email by writing to admissions@mebukicollege.example with the subject line Open day booking. You may also telephone our admissions office directly at +00 31 555 0142 between 08:30 and 17:00, Monday through Friday, to confirm your visit.',
	'i_open_f_pill' => 'Book a place',
	'i_open_f_h' => 'Book a place at an open day',
	'i_open_f_line' => 'Tell us which date suits you and which programme you are curious about. Priya Raman replies within two working days.',
	'i_con_hero_pill' => 'Contact',
	'i_con_hero_lead' => 'Our admissions office is based at 2 Orchard Row in Hollins. We welcome questions regarding programme selection, admissions procedures, observed mornings, and visits to our partner classrooms.',
	'i_con_s0_pill' => 'Find us',
	'i_con_s0_h' => 'Campus location, travel directions, and office hours',
	'i_con_s0_b_0' => 'Mebuki College is located at 2 Orchard Row, Hollins, Calder Downs. Our administrative offices are open Monday through Friday from 08:30 to 17:00. The campus is easily reached by public transport or bicycle. From Hollins railway station, bus 14 stops directly at Orchard Row, with a travel time of just 8 minutes. For those cycling, sheltered bike racks are located within our front entrance courtyard. Visitors arriving by car can find street parking nearby throughout Hollins market town. Our admissions officer, Priya Raman, is on hand during weekday hours to assist visitors, direct course inquiries, and arrange Wednesday afternoon tours of our teaching rooms and library.',
	'i_con_f0_l' => 'Address',
	'i_con_f0_v' => '2 Orchard Row, Hollins, Calder Downs',
	'i_con_f1_l' => 'Phone',
	'i_con_f1_v' => '+00 31 555 0142',
	'i_con_f2_l' => 'Email',
	'i_con_f2_v' => 'admissions@mebukicollege.example',
	'i_con_f3_l' => 'Office hours',
	'i_con_f3_v' => 'Monday–Friday 08:30–17:00',
	'i_con_g_pill' => 'Getting here',
	'i_con_g_h' => 'Bus 14 from Hollins station',
	'i_con_way' => 'Bus 14 from Hollins station takes eight minutes. There are cycle racks by the garden gate.',
	'i_con_s1_pill' => 'Write to us',
	'i_con_s1_h' => 'How can you get in touch with our admissions team?',
	'i_con_s1_b_0' => 'Prospective applicants, employers, and partner settings can reach our team using the contact form on this page. When submitting an inquiry, please indicate whether your question relates to the Diploma, Graduate Certificate, or Weekend Route, or whether you wish to schedule an informal visit. You may also write to admissions directly at admissions@mebukicollege.example with the subject Question for Mebuki College admissions, or call our office at +00 31 555 0142 between 08:30 and 17:00, Monday to Friday. Priya Raman reads every incoming message and provides detailed, individual answers within two working days to help you plan your teacher-training pathway.',
	'i_nl_hero_pill' => 'Open-day letters',
	'i_nl_hero_lead' => 'We publish four postal and digital letters each year for prospective trainees and early-childhood practitioners. Each letter contains key dates, observation notes from the floor, and updates on application deadlines.',
	'i_nl_s0_pill' => 'Four letters a year',
	'i_nl_s0_h' => 'Four seasonal dispatches from our tutors and floor',
	'i_nl_s0_b_0' => 'Our Open-day letters are published four times each year, arriving in January, March, May, and September. Rather than marketing promotional material, each edition is a thoughtful dispatch written by college tutors and partner educators. Every letter includes upcoming open-day dates, a reflective observation note drawn directly from morning floor work in our partner nurseries, and essential guidance regarding application windows and observed morning schedules. The January letter highlights winter open days; the March letter focuses on preparing your 400-word personal statement; the May dispatch shares insights on observed nursery mornings; and the September letter introduces our incoming autumn cohort and current studio research projects.',
	'i_nl_band_l' => 'January · March · May · September',
	'i_nl_band_p' => 'One letter in each season, written by a tutor on the nursery floor.',
	'i_nl_s1_pill' => 'Your details',
	'i_nl_s1_h' => 'How do we handle your details when you subscribe?',
	'i_nl_s1_b_0' => 'Joining our mailing list is simple and respectful of your privacy. To receive our four seasonal letters, enter your email address in the subscription box on this page and submit your request. We will never share your contact information with external organisations, nor will we clutter your inbox with frequent promotional messages. Our mailings are strictly limited to the four annual seasonal letters and urgent admissions deadline notifications. You may easily remove your name from our mailing list at any time by emailing admissions@mebukicollege.example. Every message is designed to provide clear, calm insights into our teacher-training programmes and partner classrooms.',
	'alt_p16' => 'The college on Orchard Row: a low brick and timber building with large windows on a quiet street of young trees.',
	'alt_p17' => 'A bright partner nursery mid-morning: children at low tables with two trainees and a nursery teacher among them.',
	'alt_p18' => 'A trainee writes a reflective journal at a window desk in the college library, beside a stack of picture books.',
	// END inner pages
);
